     9	
    10	## 1. Principles
    11	
    12	- Desktop Host imports Organizer UI only from `@repo/plugin-organizer`.
    13	- Host must not import Organizer internal source files.
    14	- Host owns native window shell, provider wiring, and AppKit drag handoff.
    15	- Organizer owns Grid business UI, item rendering, file-drop behavior, and scoped cross-window events.
    16	
    17	## 2. Public Grid Window Surface
    18	
    19	```ts
    20	export interface OrganizerGridContentProps {
    21	  gridId: string;
    22	  gridOpacity?: number;
    23	  gridBlur?: boolean;
    24	}
    25	
    26	export function OrganizerGridContent(
    27	  props: OrganizerGridContentProps
    28	): JSX.Element;
    29	```
    30	
    31	`OrganizerGridContent` is the only public content component the desktop Grid
    32	window shell may render.
    33	
    34	## 3. Host Boundary
    35	
    36	Allowed Host responsibilities:
    37	
    38	- Parse or receive `gridId` from the native window route.
    39	- Install `SettingsProvider` and drag/drop providers.
    40	- Pass presentation settings into `OrganizerGridContent`.
    41	- Handle native window dragging/chrome behavior.
    42	
    43	Disallowed Host responsibilities:
    44	
    45	- Render `SmartContainer` directly for Grid windows.
    46	- Own Grid item placement or drop semantics.
    47	- Emit Grid update/drop/close business events directly, except through the Organizer public component.
    48	
    49	## 4. Tests
    50	
    51	- `apps/desktop/src/windows/GridWindow.tsx` imports `OrganizerGridContent` from `@repo/plugin-organizer`.
    52	- `apps/desktop/src/windows/GridWindow.tsx` does not import `SmartContainer`, `GridBox`, `DesktopItem`, or Organizer internal paths.
    53	- `packages/plugin-organizer/src/index.ts` exports `OrganizerGridContent`.

